.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt TZFS.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tzfs.conf
.Nd configuration file for the tzfsd storage daemon
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa /Capabilities/Config/tzfsd.ucl
configures
.Xr tzfsd 8 .
It is a
.Xr libucl 3
document; every key is optional, and a missing file leaves the built-in
opinionated defaults in force.
Unknown keys are ignored so the schema can grow.
An existing configuration file must be a regular file owned by the daemon's
effective user and must not be writable by its group or by other users.
Symbolic links, malformed input, truncated values, invalid types, and invalid
catalog combinations are fatal startup errors.
.Sh KEYS
.Bl -tag -width ".Va ephemeral.sync"
.It Va pool
Name of the ZFS pool that backs
.Pa /Capabilities .
Setting it recomputes the root layout below unless those are overridden
explicitly.
Default
.Ql zroot .
.It Va roots.base
Base dataset for the capability storage tree.
Default
.Ql <pool>/Capabilities .
.It Va roots.persistent
Parent of persistent per-application datasets.
Default
.Ql <base>/persistent .
.It Va roots.ephemeral
Parent of ephemeral datasets, created on service start and destroyed on stop.
Default
.Ql <base>/ephemeral .
.It Va roots.templates
Parent of the flavor template datasets.
Default
.Ql <base>/.templates .
.It Va roots.mountpoint
Filesystem location of the base.
Default
.Ql /Capabilities .
.It Va ephemeral.sync
The
.Ql sync
property applied to ephemeral datasets.
Default
.Ql disabled
for throughput.
.El
.Ss Flavors
The broker's built-in flavors are only
.Ql empty
(a blank dataset) and
.Ql native
(a copy-on-write clone of the running boot environment); both are built live
on first start and need no shipped content.
OS-image flavors such as
.Ql linux
(Rocky) and
.Ql freebsd
are not built in \(em curating a distribution rootfs is a separate concern
from brokering storage.
They are contributed by the separately packaged flavor catalog,
.Xr tzfs-flavors 7 ,
which drops its own fragment under
.Pa /Capabilities/Config/tzfsd.d/ .
.Pp
The
.Va flavors
object (in this file or in a
.Pa tzfsd.d
drop-in) maps a flavor name to its settings; a name not already known is
added as a new flavor:
.Bl -tag -width ".Va enabled" -offset indent
.It Va build
How the template is populated:
.Ql live
(built from the running system),
.Ql baked
(received from a shipped send-stream), or
.Ql source
(offered only when its template has been pre-seeded; automatic source
materialization is not yet implemented).
.It Va source
Path to the baked send-stream or rootfs source.
.It Va enabled
Whether the flavor is offered.
Set to
.Ql false
to slim a deployment; for example, disabling the
.Ql linux
(Rocky) flavor drops the Red Hat userland from disk.
The flavor is then simply not offered and a request for it fails with
.Er ENOENT .
.It Va default
Marks the opinionated default flavor.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ".Pa /Capabilities/Config/tzfsd.ucl" -compact
.It Pa /Capabilities/Config/tzfsd.ucl
the file described here
.It Pa /Capabilities/Config/tzfsd.d/
flavor catalog drop-in directory; packages such as
.Sy tzfs-flavors
install additional flavor definitions here
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Turn off the bundled Linux flavor on a slimmed host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
flavors {
    linux { enabled = false; }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Back
.Pa /Capabilities
with a dedicated pool:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pool = "tank";
ephemeral { sync = "standard"; }
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libtzfsd 3 ,
.Xr trustedzfs 3 ,
.Xr tzfsctl 8 ,
.Xr tzfsd 8
